# Secrets / private config — never commit values
.env
# config/ is private by DEFAULT, and the committed examples are the only exceptions.
#
# Deny-by-default, rather than a list of the private files, because the list was the
# weaker design: it only ever covered names that had already been thought of. A file
# arriving under a name outside the enumerated patterns — an editor copy, a download
# suffix, any hand-typed variant — matched nothing and stayed untracked but visible in
# a public repo. Under the rule below a new private file is ignored because it is new,
# and only an *.example.* file, which has to be named deliberately, can be added.
#
# git will not descend into an excluded directory to find an exception under it, so
# config/seeds/ is re-admitted and then re-excluded file-by-file. Only that one
# directory is re-admitted: config/discovery/ stays excluded wholesale, which is both
# what its contents need and what scripts/check_docs.py asserts.
config/**
!config/seeds/
config/seeds/*
!config/*.example.csv
!config/*.example.yaml
!config/seeds/*.example.csv
# Personal runbook: the manual half of the system (gh commands, secrets setup).
# No secret values in it, but it is a private runbook, not project documentation.
NOTES.local.md
# The dbt seeds are filter rules, and filter rules are preferences: where the
# work may be done, which tech ranks a posting up, which ranks it down
# (ADR-0028). Materialized by `make seeds` from an Actions variable or from
# config/seeds/*.example.csv. seeds.yml stays tracked -- the schema tests are
# the mechanism, and the mechanism is public.
dbt/seeds/*.csv
*.key
*.pem
**/keyfile*.json
~/.gcp/

# Data artifacts
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.parquet
/data/

# OS / editor / runtime artifacts
.DS_Store
.vscode/
ingest_summary.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# dbt (dbt/profiles.yml is committed — it is env-var driven, no secret values)
dbt/target/
dbt/dbt_packages/
dbt/logs/
dbt/.user.yml
.vscode/
